## Hooks

Codex introduced hooks in v0.99.0 (AfterAgent) and v0.100.0 (AfterToolUse), then added an experimental hooks engine in v0.114.0 with `SessionStart` and `Stop` events.[70](#fn:72) **As of v0.124.0 (April 23, 2026), hooks are stable.**[85](#fn:162) They are now configurable inline in `config.toml` and `requirements.toml` — no more separate hook scripts file required — and they observe MCP tools alongside `apply_patch` and long-running Bash sessions. The system now covers session lifecycle and tool-level automation, closing the gap with Claude Code’s hook model.

### Available Hook Events

| Event | When It Fires | Added |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SessionStart` | Once at the beginning of a session; hook stdout is injected as startup context before the first turn | v0.114.0 `[EXPERIMENTAL]` |
| `Stop` | When the session ends | v0.114.0 `[EXPERIMENTAL]` |
| `AfterAgent` | After the agent finishes a complete turn | v0.99.0 |
| `AfterToolUse` | After each individual tool call completes | v0.100.0 |
| `UserPromptSubmit` | Before a user prompt is executed; can block or augment the prompt before it enters history | v0.116.0 `[EXPERIMENTAL]` |

### Hook Configuration

Hooks are configured in `.codex/config.toml`:

    [[hooks]]
    event = "AfterToolUse"
    command = "echo 'Tool completed' >> /tmp/codex-log.txt"

    [[hooks]]
    event = "SessionStart"
    command = "echo 'Current date: $(date +%Y-%m-%d)'"

The `SessionStart` hook’s stdout feeds into the model’s context, making it ideal for injecting dynamic information (dates, branch names, environment variables) at session start.

### Replicating Claude Code Hook Patterns

If migrating from Claude Code, here’s how to achieve similar automation:

| Claude Code Pattern | Codex Alternative |
| --- | --- |
| `PreToolUse` file blocking | AGENTS.md instructions + sandbox `read-only` mode |
| `PostToolUse` linting | `AfterToolUse` hook running your linter |
| `SessionStart` context injection | `SessionStart` hook (v0.114.0) with stdout injection |
| `Stop` notification | `Stop` hook (v0.114.0) with notification command |
| `SubagentStop` notification | `AfterAgent` hook with notification script |
| Async hooks | Not yet supported; use Cloud tasks for background work |

> **Expert tip:** As of v0.124.0 (April 23, 2026) the hooks engine is **stable**. New hook events still ship in releases — check the [Codex changelog](https://github.com/openai/codex/releases).
>
> **In-TUI hook browser (v0.129.0):** Run `/hooks` in the TUI to discover available hooks, see which are currently active, and toggle individual hooks without editing `config.toml`. Useful when troubleshooting a misbehaving plugin-bundled hook or temporarily disabling an `AfterToolUse` linter for a heads-down editing session.[89](#fn:166)
